# Plan To-Dos Self-Check

Whenever you create a plan in Plan mode (via `CreatePlan`), before presenting
it to the user you must explicitly verify that concrete, actionable to-dos
were included in the plan's frontmatter/todo list — not just prose steps in
the body.

- If the plan tool call did not include a `todos` array, stop and add one
  before finishing — don't rely on the "Proposed Fix" / "Fix" prose section
  alone as a substitute for actual to-dos.
- Each to-do should map to a concrete, checkable unit of work from the plan
  (e.g. one per file changed, one per verification step), not a single vague
  catch-all item.
- This has been missed before in this repo's workflow — treat it as a hard
  requirement, not a nice-to-have.
